From b6810bb168aae55db182774e5c0d8e2cb05caa8d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 15:20:26 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] desktop: the retry card needs the store's word that
 a turn left no reply

On 2026-11-17 a hub chat turn completed with a stored 623-char reply and Desktop
painted "Hermes ended this turn without a reply" with a Retry that would have run
the prompt twice. recoverEndedLiveTurn stamped that notice from the local
transcript whenever its stored-transcript read did not apply:
hydrateStoredSessionTranscript returns silently when the read is superseded, held
behind a replay, or fails three times, and the caller could not tell.

- hydrateStoredSessionTranscript resolves true only when a stored page was applied.
- recoverEndedLiveTurn re-reads the store (2 s, 8 s, 20 s) while no read has
  applied; only after the last one does the local transcript decide. Each
  recovery logs one [silent-turn] line with the store read's outcome.
- disproveNoReplyNotice: the turn's own stream output, or a liveness poll that
  lists it working, takes a wrong stamp back and drops the pending re-read.

Which of the two readings happened on 2026-11-17 (ended verdict during the 95 s
throttle hold, or a true end whose store read was dropped) is not established:
Desktop logged nothing then. The [silent-turn] lines now record it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
